questions.md:
A hole is to be punched out of a plate having an ultimate shear stress of 250 MPa. If the compressive stress in the punch is limited to 370 MPa, determine:
(a) the maximum thickness of the plate for which a 125 mm diameter hole can be punched;
(b) if the plate is 15 mm thick, the smallest diameter hole that can be punched.

A metal plate is to be punched with a hole; the plate can take a maximum shear stress of 150 MPa. The compressive stress in the punch is limited to 200 MPa. Determine:
i. the maximum thickness of the plate for which a 50 mm diameter hole can be punched;
ii. if the plate is 5 mm thick, the smallest diameter hole that can be punched.

A plate has an ultimate shear stress of 400 MPa. A square cut is to be punched on the plate. If the compressive stress in the cut-out is limited to 500 MPa, determine:
i. the maximum thickness of the plate for which a square of side 150 mm can be punched;
ii. if the plate is 75 mm thick, the dimension of the square cut.
